    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Brady House** emerging as a top-tier play with a 63.19 score, bolstered significantly by a favorable matchup against Woods Richardson (4.85 xERA). **House** benefits from a 19% boost due to the opposing starter\u2019s profile and a positive platoon edge, making him a cornerstone of the lineup alongside **Gunnar Henderson**. While **Henderson** faces a tougher arm in Meyer (3.69 xERA), his elite leadoff position and favorable platoon dynamics secure him a 68.57 rating, the highest among our active starters. **Nasim Nunez** also presents a compelling case at 59.76; despite batting ninth, his speed-driven profile and the soft matchup against Woods Richardson make him a critical asset for our stolen base-starved roster.\n\nOur most difficult lineup decision today involved **Coby Mayo**, who landed just shy of the start threshold with a 37.37 efficiency score. While his raw base projection remains solid, the combination of a daunting matchup against Meyer and a bottom-of-the-order assignment suppressed his output, keeping him on the bench to preserve our limited game caps. We are also closely monitoring the lineup for **Jackson Merrill**; although he is currently projected to lead off against the lefty Liberatore, his status remains \"Pending.\" Should **Merrill** be pushed down in the order or removed, we lose the 10% projection bump associated with the #1 slot, which could force a late-afternoon re-evaluation of our utility configuration. **Liam Hicks** remains a marginal start at 40.61; while he is barely above the floor, his presence in the #3 hole provides enough volume to justify the start despite the unfavorable dynamic platoon split against Povich.",
